    "Both devices remain on g531 with protected service/input READY and grant PRESENT. The same authenticated connection and original service starts were retained for approximately 254 seconds. No new A heartbeat failure, reconnect, session fault or recovery-required event after connection appears in the complete agent logs.",
    "The targeted A initial foreground request median/max changed from 19.8145/170.544ms to 1.7015/4.275ms. The measurement includes the monitor exchange and is not limited to the requester syscall.",
    "Complete A capture median/max changed from 52.5575/225.112ms to 22.685/72.027ms. This demonstrates an observed improvement in the entire measured capture interval as well as the first request; it is not merely a relabelled request-time comparison.",
    "The remaining 72.027ms capture contains 59.268ms worker activation, with first foreground request/verification only 4.275/0.508ms. Its fallback lies in the 10-to-under-100ms bucket; local request/reply delivery are 0.074/0.096ms.",
    "Foreground fallback was absent in all twelve g530 profiles but present in all twelve g531 profiles: four under 10ms and eight from 10 to under 100ms. This is a visible tradeoff of the new request path. Pending activation versus API refusal and exact fallback substage durations remain unisolated; do not claim focus ownership is complete when only the first request has returned.",
    "B readiness median/max is 25.4685/38.720ms versus 22.334/25.686ms. Every paired B startup reports a prepared worker; there is no observed cold reconstruction in these twelve profiles.",
    "B worst-input per-entry median is similar at 3.179ms versus 3.337ms, while max increased to 17.169ms from 4.941ms. Four of 354 receiver dispatches fall in the 10-to-under-100ms bucket; none reaches 100ms. Not every latency metric improved.",
    "A grant wait median/max is 43.020/71.799ms, TCP RTT estimates 5.790/23.978ms. All twelve sampled sockets have known zero timeout/retransmitted-byte deltas. These socket estimates cannot separate all network and peer processing time in grant waits.",
    "A first offer since begin median/max changed to 70.933/130.513ms from 111.2015/283.692ms. It includes physical input availability and user movement; this is not physical input-to-display latency.",
    "The nearby A runtime interval reports 37.402ms timer lateness, 27.763ms sampler lateness and 118.784ms slow control dispatch. Native activation and host scheduling remain relevant; these figures alone do not prove a CPU or GC root cause.",
